## Diagnosis

1. Confirm the alert is real: open the `{{ service.name }}-overview` dashboard and compare `{{ metric }}` with the
   same hour last week.
2. Check recent changes: `deployctl history {{ service.name }} --since 2h`. A deploy in the last hour makes
   "{{ causes[0].name | lower }}" less likely than a regression.
3. Search the logs for the error code this failure logs:

   ```bash
   kubectl -n {{ service.team }} logs deploy/{{ service.name }} --since 15m | grep {{ error_code }}
   ```

4. If `{{ metric }}` stays above {{ threshold }} for {{ minutes }} minutes, treat it as
   {{ mode.title }} and move to mitigation; below that it usually recovers on its own.
